"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[6835],{86835:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"07-moshenniki","title":"Lesson 07. Fraud: How not to lose everything in one call","sourceFingerprint":"66c16b9b445d9166699e0fb0e23e2c00fcf2477cb426df4fcb99130ef927358e","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## Fraud"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"How not to lose everything in one call"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"By this lesson you have a debt plan and the first cushion money. The main threat to it is not inflation or a falling market, but a call from an unfamiliar number."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"Bank of Russia figures: 29.3 billion RUB was stolen from bank accounts in 2025, up 6.4% from the previous year. Transactions without customer consent increased 31%. In QII 2026, customer losses reached almost 7.4 billion RUB. Banks returned only about 7%, or 514.6 million RUB."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"Central-bank statistics mainly count transactions without consent. When someone transfers voluntarily after persuasion, recovery is almost impossible and those cases usually fall outside the figures. Sber, using a broader definition, estimated fraud losses of 275–295 billion RUB in 2025."},{"id":"b006","markdown":"An uncomfortable but useful conclusion: if you make the transfer yourself, the bank probably returns nothing. Protection depends on you."},{"id":"b007","markdown":"### How almost every scheme works"},{"id":"b008","markdown":"Scenarios change monthly, but the underlying structure stays the same. Learn it rather than memorising individual stories."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"- Authority. A caller claims to be bank security, an investigator, central-bank staff, Gosuslugi, a courier, your manager or a relative."},{"id":"b010","markdown":"- Urgency. Act immediately: money is being withdrawn, a loan is being issued in your name, a parcel will be returned, or a relative is in trouble."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"- Secrecy. Tell nobody: the investigation is confidential, or the bank is involved."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"- Action. Give an SMS code, install an app, transfer to a “safe account”, withdraw cash for a courier, or take a loan to “intercept” a fraudulent one."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"If at least 2 of these 4 appear together, it is almost certainly fraud however convincing the story. The objective is preventing you from stopping to think."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"THE STRUCTURE OF ALMOST EVERY SCHEME. AUTHORITY: “BANK”, “INVESTIGATOR”. URGENCY: “RIGHT NOW”. SECRECY: “TELL NOBODY”. ACTION: CODE OR TRANSFER. 2 OUT OF 4: ALMOST CERTAINLY FRAUD. HANG UP AND CALL INDEPENDENTLY."},{"id":"b015","markdown":"### Common scenarios in 2026"},{"id":"b016","markdown":"A multi-stage attack. The “bank” reports a suspicious transaction, then “police” or “security services” join. The conversation can continue for hours or days. The ending is always a transfer to a “safe account” or a new loan to “close” a fraudulent one. Financial University experts consider this the most widespread scheme currently."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"Courier and code. “Flowers or a letter are being delivered; give the SMS code.” The code actually grants access to Gosuslugi or banking. Gosuslugi access is then used for loans or changed details. Fake bills: a QR code on a utility bill or “management-company” message leads to another account or phishing site."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"Cloned websites offer travel, tickets or goods far below market prices on apparently genuine pages. After paying, both money and purchase vanish. Manager or relative: a messenger uses a familiar photo and name, saying “officials will call, follow their instructions” or “send money urgently, I will explain later”. Voices and videos can now be forged too."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"A transfer “side job”. You receive money to your card and forward it for a percentage, or sell or “rent out” a card. This is money-mule activity, covered separately below."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"### 6 rules that stop almost everything"},{"id":"b021","markdown":"A “safe account” does not exist. Neither banks, the central bank nor police ask you to transfer funds for “protection”. Hang up on those words. Never share SMS codes or push approvals with a courier, “operator” or “Gosuslugi employee”. A code is a signature; whoever obtains it acts in your name."},{"id":"b022","markdown":"Call independently. Hang up and dial the bank number printed on your card or shown in the app. Do not use a dictated number or return the incoming call."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"Banks and public authorities do not write through foreign messengers. Since 2025 their employees have legally been prohibited from client communication through foreign messengers. A “bank” or “investigator” messaging on Telegram or WhatsApp is not the bank or investigator."},{"id":"b024","markdown":"Install nothing on request: no “protection app”, “bank update” or remote-access programme. These can give fraudsters access to your phone, banking and contactless payments. Stop. Nearly every scheme depends on haste; real banking problems can wait 10 minutes while you call independently and consult someone close."},{"id":"b025","markdown":"Fraud or not? Seven situations."},{"id":"b026","markdown":"“Bank security” calls: someone is trying to withdraw from your card, so urgently transfer everything to a safe account."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"Everything is fine. Fraud."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"### What to arrange in advance"},{"id":"b029","markdown":"Many protections are one-time tasks. A voluntary credit restriction, covered in lesson 4: choose full restriction if no borrowing is planned. A SIM-card restriction through Gosuslugi or a public-services centre prevents mobile contracts in your name without personal attendance. Set it online; removal requires a centre visit, preventing remote fraudster removal."},{"id":"b030","markdown":"Opt out of mass calls and messages. The law allows refusing advertising calls and messages through your operator. Fewer unfamiliar calls make suspicious ones easier to notice. A second key for Gosuslugi: enable confirmed sign-in and check which devices and apps can access the account."},{"id":"b031","markdown":"Keep the cushion separate from daily money. Use a bank without a spending card linked to it and keep it off the app’s main screen. Compromising one card then leaves the cushion protected."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"A “second hand” for parents. Since September 1, 2025, banks can appoint a trusted person to confirm transfers. You choose which operations need approval, and money waits for it. Without a response within 12 hours, payment is declined. The person receives no account access. This is especially useful for older relatives; each bank sets its own activation terms."},{"id":"b033","markdown":"### Money mules: imprisonment for a “side job”"},{"id":"b034","markdown":"Fraudsters route stolen money through chains of other people’s cards to obscure tracing. The owners are money mules, recruited among students and teenagers in job chats and vacancy websites: “receive transfers and keep 5%”."},{"id":"b035","markdown":"Since 2025, Article 187 of Russia’s Criminal Code provides criminal liability. Giving fraudsters your card or access, or transferring on their instructions, can mean up to 3 years in prison. Using or buying others’ cards for such operations can mean up to 6 years and a fine up to 1 million RUB. The central bank also maintains a mule database, whose listed people face bank restrictions on transfers and online banking."},{"id":"b036","markdown":"Never hand over your card, banking account or SIM cards for any amount. Explain this to children and younger relatives, who are at risk."},{"id":"b037","markdown":"### If it has already happened"},{"id":"b038","markdown":"Act in the first hours."},{"id":"b039","markdown":"- Call the bank using the card or app number and block both card and app access. For an unauthorised debit, notify the bank by the end of the day after the transaction notification. The law then requires investigation and, in most cases, reimbursement."},{"id":"b040","markdown":"- If you transferred voluntarily, still call immediately; sometimes the transfer can be stopped. If the recipient was already in the central bank’s fraud database, the law requires the bank itself to refund the money."},{"id":"b041","markdown":"- File a police report in person or through Gosuslugi. Without it, banks and courts can do little."},{"id":"b042","markdown":"- Check credit history and Gosuslugi for new loans or altered details. Set restrictions if not already in place."},{"id":"b043","markdown":"- Warn people close to you if a messenger was hacked; fraudulent messages will target them."},{"id":"b044","markdown":"There is no reason for shame. Professionals write these scripts and deceive lawyers, bankers and IT specialists too. Faster action gives a greater chance of recovering something."},{"id":"b045","markdown":"### The essentials"},{"id":"b046","markdown":"- If you transferred voluntarily, the bank is unlikely to refund. Protection depends on you."},{"id":"b047","markdown":"- Almost every scheme combines authority, urgency, secrecy and action involving money or a code."},{"id":"b048","markdown":"- Safe accounts do not exist. Never share codes; call independently using the card number."},{"id":"b049","markdown":"- Set credit and SIM restrictions in advance, keep the cushion separate and arrange a trusted “second hand” for parents."},{"id":"b050","markdown":"- Giving someone your card for money can be a criminal offence."},{"id":"b051","markdown":"Debts are controlled and the cushion built and protected. Next lesson examines making money work."}],"terms":[{"id":"inflyatsiya","term":"Inflation","definition":"A rise in the general price level. In practice: there is more money and the same quantity of goods, so each item costs more. You have not become richer; price tags have simply risen."},{"id":"kreditnaya-istoriya","term":"Credit history","definition":"A record of how you repaid loans. A poor or absent history means rejection or a rate above the market. An empty history is worse than a history of repaid loans."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"07-moshenniki-q1","q":"“Bank security” urgently asks you to transfer to a safe account because money is being stolen. What should you do?","options":["Transfer before it is too late","Hang up and call the bank using the number on the card","Transfer half to test it"],"correct":1},{"id":"07-moshenniki-q2","q":"A courier requests an SMS code to confirm flower delivery. What is most likely happening?","options":["An attempt to access your Gosuslugi or bank account","A standard delivery procedure","The mobile operator checking your number"],"correct":0},{"id":"07-moshenniki-q3","q":"A side-job chat offers 5% for receiving and forwarding transfers through your card. What is the risk?","options":["None: ordinary part-time work","Only a one-day card block","Criminal liability under Article 187 and entry in the central bank’s money-mule database"],"correct":2}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);